Alembic revisions, run through Flask-Migrate.

    flask db upgrade                 apply every pending revision
    flask db downgrade -1            step back one revision
    flask db migrate -m "message"    autogenerate a revision from model changes
    flask db current                 show the revision the database is on

Autogenerated revisions are always reviewed before being committed. Alembic does not
detect every change - notably it does not diff check constraints or the members of an
existing enum type - so anything it misses is added to the revision by hand.
